WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.070
Hi.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.431
My name is Ken Shotts.

00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:04.669
&gt;&gt; And I'm Neil Malhotra.

00:00:04.669 --> 00:00:09.340
And we would like to introduce you to
the course on Values-Based Leadership.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.616
&gt;&gt; This course is about how
to lead with our values and

00:00:12.616 --> 00:00:15.192
implement them in our organizations.

00:00:15.192 --> 00:00:20.168
Gaining a better understanding of our own
value systems can make us more effective

00:00:20.168 --> 00:00:24.220
managers and help us be the kinds
of leaders people want to follow.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.700
Clarifying our value systems will also
help us make better decisions for

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.008
the benefit of key stakeholders,
such as shareholders, employees,

00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:36.184
costumers, and society at large.

00:00:36.184 --> 00:00:40.716
&gt;&gt; This course will address several key
questions in values based leadership.

00:00:40.716 --> 00:00:44.630
Should we make decisions
based on our gut intuitions?

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:48.125
How can we design organizations
to prevent ethical lapses?

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:51.400
What is the role of companies in society?

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.251
How can we manage trade-offs and
weigh the consequences of our actions?

00:00:55.251 --> 00:00:59.689
And how can we engage in
perspective-taking to build more inclusive

00:00:59.689 --> 00:01:02.050
and fair organizations?

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.319
&gt;&gt; These questions are complicated,
and they don't have easy answers.

00:01:06.319 --> 00:01:10.759
The goal of this course,
is to engage with these stony issues, so

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:13.526
that we can better lead with our values.

00:01:13.526 --> 00:01:18.176
By the end of this course, you will
clarify your own values, gain a better

00:01:18.176 --> 00:01:22.905
understanding of the diversity of
ethical perspectives in business, and

00:01:22.905 --> 00:01:27.950
learn how to lead and design organizations
to implement your personal values.

